- op: create  # a8e6
  at: '2026-08-10T20:15:02Z'  # a8e6
  by: agent  # a8e6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a8e6
  clock: 1  # a8e6
  nonce: a8e6  # a8e6
  data:  # a8e6
    kind: invariant  # a8e6
    title: "python puts a module-qualified name in the NAME slot on some call edges (sys.stderr, os.path), doubling any module+name composition"  # a8e6
    status: violated  # a8e6
    priority: 3  # a8e6
    parent:  # a8e6
    tags:  # a8e6
    - analysis_quality  # a8e6
    - io_boundary  # a8e6
    - taint  # a8e6
    isbefore: []  # a8e6
    duplicate_of: []  # a8e6
    not_duplicate_of: []  # a8e6
    pr_ref:  # a8e6
    description: "MEASURED 2026-08-10 (dev 52acec99be), via scripts/measure-call-escape-cause.py\non hypergumbo itself; positive control passed (596,712 edges offered / 318,012\naccepted / 69 summary entries / 29,348 callees_at / 171 escape events).\n\nTHE DEFECT. Some python `calls` edges carry a MODULE-QUALIFIED name in the NAME\nslot while the module slot holds only the first segment, so any consumer that\ncomposes module + \".\" + name doubles the prefix. Read through production's own\nhelpers (_module_from_symbol_path / _extract_callee_name / _qualified_callee):\n\n  dst                                        module   name         composed key\n  python:sys:0-0:sys.stderr:external_symbol  sys      sys.stderr   sys.sys.stderr\n  python:os:0-0:os.path:external_symbol      os       os.path      os.os.path\n  python:os.path:0-0:join:external_symbol    os.path  join         os.path.join   (correct)\n  python:os:0-0:makedirs:external_symbol     os       makedirs     os.makedirs    (correct)\n\nSo the analyzer is INCONSISTENT about which slot carries the qualifier for the\nsame repo in the same run.\n\nWHY THE CATALOGUE CANNOT ABSORB IT. io_primitives/python.yaml declares\n`module: sys, name: stderr, kind: attribute` (boundary `logging`). A lookup keyed\non name=`sys.stderr` cannot equal name=`stderr` no matter what is added to the\nYAML. This is why it is filed as a slot defect and not as a catalogue gap -- the\nINV-busis 4a bucket counted these two keys as \"catalogue gap\" and they are not.\n\nCONSEQUENCE TODAY IS SMALL AND IS STATED RATHER THAN INFLATED. _qualified_callee\nhas exactly ONE caller (_catalogue_key_for_edge), which feeds only the ADR-0017\nsection 4 summary lookup -- and that path is measured INERT (see INV-busis's\n2026-08-10 ceiling note: closing every escape site moved 0 findings). Separately,\nthe generated reach probe shows all 9 attribute-kind python primitives ARE\nreachable when written as a plain `sys.stderr` reference, so the ordinary form is\nnot affected. The malformed dsts arise on some other emission path.\n\nNOT DIAGNOSED: which py.py emit site produces the doubled name slot. A minimal\nfixture (`print(msg, file=sys.stderr)` alone) produces NO edge at all, so it does\nnot reproduce in isolation and the producing path was not localised. Do not treat\nthe mechanism as known."  # a8e6
    fields:  # a8e6
      statement: "A call edge's NAME slot must carry the callee name alone. python emits name='sys.stderr' with module='sys' and name='os.path' with module='os', so composing module + '.' + name yields 'sys.sys.stderr' / 'os.os.path' and no catalogue entry can match. python.yaml declares module='sys', name='stderr'."  # a8e6
      root_cause: "MEASURED 2026-08-10 (dev 52acec99be), via scripts/measure-call-escape-cause.py\non hypergumbo itself; positive control passed (596,712 edges offered / 318,012\naccepted / 69 summary entries / 29,348 callees_at / 171 escape events).\n\nTHE DEFECT. Some python `calls` edges carry a MODULE-QUALIFIED name in the NAME\nslot while the module slot holds only the first segment, so any consumer that\ncomposes module + \".\" + name doubles the prefix. Read through production's own\nhelpers (_module_from_symbol_path / _extract_callee_name / _qualified_callee):\n\n  dst                                        module   name         composed key\n  python:sys:0-0:sys.stderr:external_symbol  sys      sys.stderr   sys.sys.stderr\n  python:os:0-0:os.path:external_symbol      os       os.path      os.os.path\n  python:os.path:0-0:join:external_symbol    os.path  join         os.path.join   (correct)\n  python:os:0-0:makedirs:external_symbol     os       makedirs     os.makedirs    (correct)\n\nSo the analyzer is INCONSISTENT about which slot carries the qualifier for the\nsame repo in the same run.\n\nWHY THE CATALOGUE CANNOT ABSORB IT. io_primitives/python.yaml declares\n`module: sys, name: stderr, kind: attribute` (boundary `logging`). A lookup keyed\non name=`sys.stderr` cannot equal name=`stderr` no matter what is added to the\nYAML. This is why it is filed as a slot defect and not as a catalogue gap -- the\nINV-busis 4a bucket counted these two keys as \"catalogue gap\" and they are not.\n\nCONSEQUENCE TODAY IS SMALL AND IS STATED RATHER THAN INFLATED. _qualified_callee\nhas exactly ONE caller (_catalogue_key_for_edge), which feeds only the ADR-0017\nsection 4 summary lookup -- and that path is measured INERT (see INV-busis's\n2026-08-10 ceiling note: closing every escape site moved 0 findings). Separately,\nthe generated reach probe shows all 9 attribute-kind python primitives ARE\nreachable when written as a plain `sys.stderr` reference, so the ordinary form is\nnot affected. The malformed dsts arise on some other emission path.\n\nNOT DIAGNOSED: which py.py emit site produces the doubled name slot. A minimal\nfixture (`print(msg, file=sys.stderr)` alone) produces NO edge at all, so it does\nnot reproduce in isolation and the producing path was not localised. Do not treat\nthe mechanism as known."  # a8e6
- op: discuss  # df9d
  at: '2026-09-01T05:45:15Z'  # df9d
  by: agent  # df9d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # df9d
  clock: 2  # df9d
  nonce: df9d  # df9d
  message: "ENRICHMENT from the module-key concept audit, 2026-09-01 (cadence). Full write-up:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-module-key_09012026.md\n\nTHIS ITEM IS FILED AS PYTHON-ONLY AND THE DEFECT IS CROSS-LANGUAGE. Measured over\n65,187 external refs on a 21-repo / 10-language cohort, every repo cold in its own\nXDG_CACHE_HOME:\n\n  3,515 external refs carry a NAME slot that re-states the module qualifier\n    by language: java 2421, python 543, go 363, javascript 116, bash 43, c 18, typescript 11\n    299 of those miss a catalogue row that the BARE name would hit\n    by language: python 116, java 57, bash 43, go 39, javascript 25, c 18, typescript 1\n\nTHE GATE ALREADY REFUSES THE TRAPS, which is the reassuring half and needs saying\nbecause it bounds any fix: after unqualification, os.path -> None,\n./constants.open -> None, ../js/phoenix/ajax.request -> None,\nsre_constants.error -> None, urllib.parse -> None, reflect.String -> None. The F3\ngate and module filter reject every first-party and non-primitive case I checked.\n\nHOW MANY BOUNDARIES ARE ACTUALLY LOST -- reported honestly, because presence is\nnot reachability. Of the 233 that resolve, 175 are ALREADY TAGGED in the same repo\nthrough another edge. That leaves 58 genuinely new boundaries:\n    java System.out x51, java System.err x3, python datetime.now x4\nThe dedup key was a coarse (repo, lang, primitive-name), which biases toward\n\"already tagged\", so 58 is a LOWER BOUND.\n\nJAVA'S HALF IS INV-fofoj, AND THE TWO ITEMS ARE ONE DEFECT. INV-fofoj's stated\njava root cause -- \"emits java:external:0-0:in.read rather than resolving\njava.lang.System\" -- is not what the shipped analyzer does. Measured on a\npurpose-built probe:\n\n    module_attr_ref  dst=java:System:0-0:System.in:external_symbol  name=System.in\n\nThe module slot DOES resolve (System, which _module_matches matches against\njava.lang.System via the suffix arm), and module_attr_ref IS in\ntag_io_boundaries' call_types, so the edge reaches the pipeline. The whole failure\nis that the NAME slot is module-qualified -- exactly this item. Two-line\ndifferential through the production classifier:\n\n    name=\"System.in\"  -> None\n    name=\"in\"         -> IoPrimitive(boundary='ipc_recv', module='java.lang.System',\n                                     name='in', kind='attribute')\n\nSo java's ONLY ipc_recv row is lost to this item's defect, not to a\n\"not-a-function-application\" shape. Recommend re-scoping this item to all seven\nlanguages and cross-referencing INV-fofoj rather than fixing python alone.\n\nINERT vs BROKEN, reported separately per the standing rule: the mechanism is\nconfirmed LIVE by System.out/System.err (54 recoveries on this cohort), while\njava's System.in -- the SOURCE row and INV-fofoj's named instance -- is inert here\nonly because no cohort repo reads stdin in java. Same mechanism, different luck."  # df9d
